Krim Landau, LLC performs a variety of accounting, tax preparation, tax planning, tax and business consulting, financial and auditing services. We assist our clients in all aspects to fulfill their financial potential. Due to our many contacts in the banking industry, we can facilitate debt and equity financing, organize buy sell-agreements, and effectively execute lucrative succession planning.
We are also adept at assisting our clients with retirement and estate planning, accounting program consulting, and in representation before the IRS on behalf of our clients.
					 Commitment to Quality 
							
			
			
		
						
Krim Landau, LLC is a member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the New Jersey Society of Certified Public Accountants (NJSCPA). One of the requirements of membership is a rigorous review every three years of our firm’s Quality Control
Policy, conducted by specially trained CPAs from other firms. This evaluation entails a thorough review of our work to ensure that our firm adheres to the highest level of professional standards. Since our inception in 1990, every review of our firm has resulted in the determination that Krim Landau adheres to the highest level of professional standards.
Robert S. Krim is a tax specialist and a founding partner of our firm. His prior experience includes 10 years with the Internal Revenue Service as a Revenue Agent, Revenue Agent Instructor, and Conferee. He has a unique understanding of tax law a creative approach in designing beneficial tax strategies. In addition to being licensed as an accountant, Robert is a Certified Financial Planner, Enrolled Agent, and Accredited Tax Advisor.
Founder / Partner
Scott Landau is a founding partner of our firm. With a diverse professional background, he brings a wealth of experience in developing innovative financial strategies and alternative solutions tailored to meet the unique needs of businesses across industries. A graduate of Villanova University and an avid golfer, Scott is also a proud member of both the New Jersey Society of Certified Public Accountants (NJSCPA) and the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA).
Founder / Managing Partner
Marlena is a dedicated accounting professional who expertly handles clients of all sizes, ensuring tailored solutions that meet their unique needs. With extensive knowledge of QuickBooks Online and a strong background in bookkeeping and accounting, she combines strategic insight with a commitment to exceptional service. Marlena's ability to build lasting relationships and deliver results makes her a valued partner for businesses looking to grow and succeed.
Amanda has been with Krim Landau since 2015 With a background in business administration and studies in accounting, Amanda combines strong organizational skills with a proactive approach to optimizing firm operations and client satisfaction.
