Pennance Mill Farm is a delightful family-run campsite nestled on a working dairy farm just under two miles from the lively seaside town of Falmouth. It’s set across three sheltered, south-facing meadows with spacious pitches perfect for tents, tourers, and motorhomes, alongside cosy self-catering chalets and shepherd’s huts. The vibe here is laid-back and welcoming, with well-kept facilities including toilets, warm showers, electric hook-ups, and a small farm shop stocking groceries and local goodies. Families will appreciate the children’s play area packed with swings, slides, and climbing frames, plus seasonal activities like family discos, games nights, and skittle evenings, making it a charming spot for campers seeking a peaceful yet friendly rural escape.
The location is a real treat for outdoor lovers and explorers. Just a short trip away are stunning Cornish beaches perfect for paddling and picnics, while numerous coastal and countryside walks invite you to soak in the breathtaking views of Cornwall’s Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty. On-site, you can enjoy a round of pitch and putt or hop over to Falmouth to explore its vibrant harbour, shops, and cafés. Nearby, there’s also cycle hire and opportunities for canoeing, providing plenty of ways to get active or simply unwind amidst nature’s beauty. Whether it’s adventure or relaxation you’re after, Pennance Mill offers a brilliant base to savour the best of Cornwall’s coast and countryside.
